# 7. AI VIDEO CLIPPING ENGINE

This is the central feature of the platform.

Build a genuine AI-powered clipping workflow.

The user should be able to select a video and request automatic clip generation.

### Processing pipeline

STEP 1: VIDEO ANALYSIS

Extract:
- Video metadata.
- Audio information.
- Representative video frames.
- Speech content.
- Scene changes where possible.

STEP 2: TRANSCRIPTION

Implement speech-to-text integration.

Use an available free transcription option where possible.

Support timestamped transcripts.

If a transcription service is unavailable, provide an honest fallback, such as transcript upload or manual transcript entry.

Do not generate fake transcripts.

STEP 3: GEMINI AI ANALYSIS

Integrate Gemini through secure server-side API calls.

Use the model configured in the application settings and verify that it is available under the user's free API allowance.

Ask Gemini to analyze the transcript and representative frames.

Identify:
- Interesting statements.
- Strong opening hooks.
- Educational moments.
- Important explanations.
- Funny moments.
- Emotional moments.
- Powerful reactions.
- Complete stories.
- Valuable discussions.

STEP 4: CLIP SELECTION

Generate candidate clips with:

- Start timestamp.
- End timestamp.
- Duration.
- Suggested title.
- Short description.
- Opening hook.
- Main topic.
- Engagement potential score.
- Reason for selection.

The AI must select complete, understandable moments.

Avoid cutting sentences in half.

Avoid clips that begin or end abruptly.

Avoid unnecessary silence.

Avoid generating several nearly identical clips.

STEP 5: CLIP GENERATION

Use FFmpeg.wasm to generate actual video clips.

Support:
- Start and end trimming.
- Video resizing.
- Video cropping.
- Audio processing.
- Subtitle rendering.
- Export encoding.

Every generated clip must correspond to its actual source timestamps.

Do not create fake downloadable clip records.

### Clip duration

Allow users to choose their own duration.

Provide editable minimum and maximum duration settings.

Do not impose an artificial fixed duration.

Validate that the selected duration does not exceed the original video's length.

